## Test coverage (`socket-level-wrapper-MQC/examples/`)

New tests under the existing `examples/` harness, runnable via
`make -f Makefile.tools test`:

1. **happy-clear** — connect/accept clear mode end-to-end, verify
   data-plane echo round-trip.
2. **happy-encrypted** — same, encrypted mode.
3. **neg-role-swap** — capture a client ClientHello, replay it as
   a ServerHello (swap field positions); verifier must reject
   because the role tag in the transcript hash differs.
4. **neg-cert-swap** — alter `cert_index` after the signature was
   made; verify must fail (transcript binds it).
5. **neg-kem-swap** — swap `kem_pub` after sign; verify must fail.
6. **neg-empty-ctx-replay** — sign a transcript with the correct
   bytes but `ctx=NULL,0` (the old protocol); the new verifier with
   `ctx="mqc-hndshk/v1\n\x00"` must reject.  Proves domain
   separation works.
7. **neg-mqc-id-replay** — present the pre-fix encrypted-mode
   server-side blob (literal `"mqc-id:N"` signature) to the new
   verifier; must be rejected.
8. **neg-version-mismatch** — `version=1` in JSON but signature
   computed over `version=0`; verify must fail.
9. **neg-suite-mismatch** — `suite="OTHER"`; verify must fail.
10. **neg-mode-downgrade** — capture an encrypted-mode ClientHello,
    strip `mode`, present to server; reject.

---

## Migration runbook (factsorlie.com, port 8446)

Single deployment, single MTC log, no external 8446 clients.

1. On the dev box: build, install, `make -f Makefile.tools test`
   (all 10 tests above must pass), `make -f Makefile.tools` clean
   (zero warnings, per CLAUDE.md guardrail).
2. Spec edits committed to the same branch as the code.
3. SSH to factsorlie.com:
   - `git pull` the new branch.
   - `./make-all.sh`.
   - `sudo systemctl restart mtc-ca.service`.
   - `journalctl -u mtc-ca.service -f` — verify clean restart, no
     MQC handshake errors against itself for the recosign / loopback
     paths.
4. The MTC client tools (`show-tpm`, `bootstrap_ca`, `bootstrap_leaf`,
   `admin_recosign`) all link the same updated `libmqc.a`.  Once
   redeployed they all speak new-MQC.
5. Smoke test from the dev box (which has now also been upgraded):
   `echo hi | mqc --encode --env --no-cache | mqc --decode --env
   --no-cache` should print `hi`.
6. End-to-end: `show-tpm --verify` against factsorlie.com:8446
   succeeds.

If a CA-internal job is mid-run during the cutover its existing TCP
connection holds the old protocol bytes in flight and will fail at
the next handshake; this is acceptable (the jobs are short and
re-runnable).

